// HONESTY-SWEEP (2026-11-07) - probe Q-HS5 for the capture lane (W6-T9 review N3; sibling of W6-U1 rows U03-U04, U08).
// Queue: docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-07-honesty-sweep.md
// Chart: AMEX:SPY 1D, AFTER THE CLOSE.
// The question: does Pine COMPILE a call that hands an array<int> (matrix<int>, map<string, int>) to a parameter
// declared with `float` elements? A compile error is the reading: record its text and line, comment that row
// out, and capture the rest. The script may not compile at all; that is the first reading.
//
//   A01  plain function f(array<float> id) called with an array<int>
//   A02  method m(array<float> id) called as ai.m() on an array<int>
//   A03  method mm(matrix<float> id) on a matrix<int>
//   A04  method mp(map<string, float> id) on a map<string, int>
//   A05  CONTROL: f called with an array<float>
//@version=6
indicator("vw-hs5-int-array-float-param", overlay = false)
f(array<float> id) =>
    id.size() + 1
method m(array<float> id) =>
    id.size() + 2
method mm(matrix<float> id) =>
    id.rows() + 3
method mp(map<string, float> id) =>
    id.size() + 4
var array<int> ai = array.from(1, 2, 3)
var array<float> af = array.from(1.5, 2.5)
var matrix<int> mi = matrix.new<int>(2, 2, 1)
var map<string, int> pi = map.new<string, int>()
plot(f(ai), "A01")
plot(ai.m(), "A02")
plot(mi.mm(), "A03")
plot(pi.mp(), "A04")
plot(f(af), "A05")
